==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|rightuous}}, {{l|en|rightwise}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|en|rightuous}}, {{m|en|rightwose}}, {{m|en|rightwos}}, {{m|en|rightwise}}, from {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|rightwise}}, {{m|enm|rightwis}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|rihtwīs||righteous, just, right, justifiable}}, corresponding to {{suffix|right|wise|lang=en}} (with assimilation of second element to {{m|en|-ous}}), or to {{compound|right|wise|t2=way, manner|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{m|sco|richtwis||righteous}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|rehtwīsic||righteous, just}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|réttvíss||righteous, just}}. Compare also {{l|en|thefteous}}, {{l|en|mighteous}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈraɪtʃəs/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-righteous.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aɪtʃəs|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[free|Free]] from [[sin]] or [[guilt]].
# [[moral|Moral]] and [[virtuous]], suggesting [[sanctimonious]].
# [[justified|Justified]] [[morally]].
#: '''''righteous''' rage''
# {{label|en|slang|US}} [[awesome|Awesome]].

